    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). The change is complete and green.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe spec: when a create/update owner request includes `birthDate` (ISO), return `ageBand` computed as the owner's age **on `registrationDate`** \u2014 `MINOR` (<18), `ADULT` (18\u201364), `SENIOR` (65+).\n\nFollowing the OfficeFloor/PetClinic conventions (DTOs generated from OpenAPI, derived response fields computed in the MapStruct mapper), I made six coordinated changes:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added `birthDate` (`string`/`date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema and a read-only `ageBand` enum (`MINOR`/`ADULT`/`SENIOR`) to the `Owner` schema. This regenerates `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` at build time.\n\n2. **`Owner` entity** \u2014 added a persisted `birthDate` (`@Column(name = \"birth_date\")`) field with getter/setter, so it survives the POST\u2192GET round-trip the test exercises.\n\n3. **Schema SQL (all four DBs: hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres)** \u2014 added a `birth_date DATE` column. This was essential: tests run under the `hsqldb` profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in `schema.sql`.\n\n4. **`AgeBand` helper** (new class) \u2014 derives `OwnerDto.AgeBandEnum` via `Period.between(birthDate, registrationDate).getYears()`, returning `null` when `birthDate` is absent so the field is simply omitted.\n\n5. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"ageBand\", expression = \"\u2026AgeBand.of(owner)\")`, matching the existing derived-field pattern. `birthDate` itself maps through automatically by name.\n\n6. **`ApplyOwner`** \u2014 copies `birthDate` onto the entity on PUT, so updates carry the field too (POST already flows through MapStruct's `toOwner`).\n\nThe target test `coreDerivesAgeBand` (birthDate `1990-01-01` \u2192 `ADULT`) passes, and the overall build is green.",
